      "message": "[warning] Line 451: 🟡 `recheckSpelling()` still tokenizes and checks every word for locales that have no installed dictionary (e.g., peer-sent `lang` values not present locally). Because `spellIn()` treats missing dictionaries as \"word is correct\", this becomes wasted O(total_words) work on each recheck and can noticeably impact large documents. Short-circuit these runs before `findWords()` (for example, skip when the locale is not in `root.spellLanguages`), or add an explicit availability check in `SpellCheckAdapter` and bail out early.",
